.TH SOFT 1 "October 2026" "Bison BASIC" "User Manual"
.SH NAME
soft \- Applesoft BASIC interpreter and compiler
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B soft
[
.B -d
]
[
.I file.bas
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B soft
is a lightweight Applesoft BASIC interpreter and compiler. It allows interactive execution (immediate mode) or compilation of BASIC programs into C code, which is then compiled and executed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -d
Enables parser debugging mode (sets YYDEBUG=1).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B RUN
Compiles the current program to C and executes it.
.TP
.B SAVE \fIfile\fP
Saves the compiled C code lines to a file.
.TP
.B LOAD \fIfile\fP
Loads a BASIC source file into memory.
.TP
.B EXEC \fIfile\fP
Executes/includes a BASIC source file interactively.
.TP
.B CATALOG \fR(or\fP CAT\fR)\fP
Lists files in the current directory.
.TP
.B PREFIX \fI[path]\fP
Displays or changes the current working directory.
.TP
.B PLOT \fIx, y\fP
Plots a point on the screen using ANSI escape sequences.
.TP
.B DATA \fR...\fP
Stores data values for READ statements.
.TP
.B READ \fIvar\fP
Reads values from DATA statements into variables.
.SH AUTHORS
Written by the Bison BASIC team.
